Hear ye!  Hear ye!  Beta players and server admins wanted!

I've created, with help from darkfred on the server end, a new telnet client 
for playing nethack.  It works in 32 bit Windows for the client.  Sorry, 
Linux users, you'll have to wait for a: me to develop more savvy programming 
under X, or b: someone with more experience willing to port the app.

The new client features the ability on all servers to use the mouse.  Click 
on a spot, and it will send the travel command, and select the location for 
you, or use any of the commands in the game that require selecting a 
location and then double click the spot with the mouse.

Also featured are the meta commands Alt-S to sit, Alt-P to pray, etc.  All 
the commands that work with number_pad enabled are mapped in the client, and 
conveniently listed in a drop down menu.

Finally, and the big one, is the ability to render the game in default 
nethack tiles.  On any server, this will bring up a scrolling message window 
that keeps track of the last 100 messages that were sent, a status window at 
the bottom showing your stats, and a tiled view of the dungeon where any 
feature that is uniquely represented by a character and a color is rendered 
as tile, with the rest in their ASCII representation.

On a server that incorporates the patch, included on the web page, the 
client will render the dungeon in full tiles.  No more guessing if that 
purple h is a dwarven king or a MFing MMF.  Or that purple @ that you meet 
in the endgame?  Elvenking or Wizard?

The website with the beta and the patch are located at 
http://www.geocities.com/jdhilts@sbcglobal.net/

